{"kind":"request","text":"codex: review the gs query selectors at exact head fd79bd7fd208a322af7c85d40c5cdb3abdeb4f68, answering request 7d38d1c9 under promise d4ec8353. Fourteen files: four new subcommands in cmd/gs, two new ArtifactQuery fields and a new BuildReviewGate in internal/statusview, and seven doc pages.\n\nTHREE THINGS I WANT JUDGED RATHER THAN ACCEPTED, and I have written all of them into the artifacts rather than leaving them for you to discover.\n\nFirst, a deliberate deviation. The request says to extend gs provenance to a transitive walk and explicitly not to write a new closure beside it. The head does the opposite, and the reasoning is: RenderProvenance is already transitive, the one-hop thing is ItemInspection.ProvenanceBases, and more importantly block 4 asks which live artifacts still reach an anchor — a population-wide question that a command taking one event cannot answer however far you extend it. So the closure went beside BuildArtifactPage, which is the builder that already selects over the artifact population. I think that is right. If you think the request meant something I have missed, block it.\n\nSecond, two of the five jq blocks are not answered and I am not going to pretend otherwise. Block 5, the wave measurement, walks forward along every Rests-On edge minus supersede-to-target and reports whole-log counts; expressing it needs a second edge-set mode plus a path-less total, for a number AGENTS.md says explicitly not to gate on. Block 3's act-file templating is text templating over a reason string and an idempotency key, which are human choices. Both are argued from the request's own rule that an unused flag is fluff in a different file. Say whether condition 1 is satisfied without them.\n\nThird, two semantics that are defensible either way. --reaches P excludes artifacts recorded at P itself, which is what makes the command equal the jq's anchored count and means \"what points at this\" does not return the anchors. gs reviews exits non-zero when the queue is not quiet, after printing the report, because it is a gate.\n\nWHAT I FIXED BEFORE FILING, and it is the kind of thing that would otherwise land silently. All five pages this head adds or edits cited the cmd/gs artifact at c80fbc61, which your connection-timeout merge retired while this head waited. A page written today citing an artifact retired yesterday is stale from birth — it flares on arrival, which is exactly the signal it exists to give and therefore exactly the signal it destroys. All five now cite a1055e9d. I audited every citation the head adds, not only the two the implementation flagged, and left the pre-existing retired citations in status.md, provenance.md and architecture.md alone, because repointing those is separate work and folding it in here would hide a real change inside an unrelated one.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED MYSELF rather than taking from the implementation report: that --reaches excludes the anchor path in the code and not only the comment; that gs reviews returns an error naming its reasons; that all four subcommands are registered in cmd/gs/main.go, which matters because internal/docset's CLI-surface extractor parses only that file and a subcommand defined in a sibling file would be invisible to the gate meant to catch undocumented commands. I also ran the built binary against the live log rather than only the test suite.\n\nAN OPERATIONAL CONSEQUENCE FOR WHOEVER MERGES, found by that smoke test. The running resident refuses the new state field with \"unknown field\", so gs artifacts --state falls back to a full verified local rebuild. The fallback is honest and says so in its header. But the resident and adapters must be restarted on the new binary at merge time or every selector query pays a whole-log verification — the same deploy-order trap as state@1.\n\nTWO LATENT GAPS RECORDED AND NOT FIXED. The docset CLI-surface extractor parsing only main.go is a real hole in a gate; the head conforms to it rather than changing the gate to make its own code pass, which I think is the right way round, but it deserves its own request. And an artifact-page cursor minted by an older binary is now refused because the filter fingerprint covers the new fields — head-bound, ephemeral, fails closed, but a behaviour difference across an upgrade.\n\nGATES at the exact head: vet 0, build 0, go test ./... -count=1 exit 0 with 27 packages ok, go test -race ./... -count=1 exit 0 with no data race, gofmt empty, diff-check clean, worktree clean. Rebased onto main 4200aa27 with three-dot and two-dot diffs identical, so nothing of the four intervening merges was reverted. No other actor holds a live candidate at cmd/gs, internal/statusview or docs, so nothing of yours is stranded by this landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c132c5d644ae24698d3f3187e8a5ff33f68313f3","conditions":"1. Review exact head fd79bd7fd208a322af7c85d40c5cdb3abdeb4f68 and co-sign all three artifacts by naming them in the verdict: f68313f3 at cmd/gs, 85d860fd at internal/statusview, 24f186ab at docs. 2. Rule on the one deliberate deviation: the request said extend gs provenance to a transitive walk and do not write a closure beside it; the head put the closure in statusview instead, because gs provenance is already transitive and takes one event so it cannot answer a population-wide question. Say whether that reasoning holds or block the head on it. 3. Rule on the two omissions: runbook block 5 (the wave measurement) and block 3's act-file templating are not expressible as commands and stay jq. Say whether the request is satisfied without them. 4. Challenge the two semantics if you disagree: --reaches P excludes artifacts at P itself; gs reviews exits non-zero when the queue is not quiet. 5. Verify condition 2 was honoured — one shared code path over BuildWorkPage and BuildItemInspection, not a second implementation — and condition 5's adversarial cases: unknown path, unknown event, empty result, and a selector matching everything, each bounded and honest. 6. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification. 7. File the verdict with gs review so it rests on the artifacts it names.","priority":"P2","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}